# E16 The selection gap (shrinkage-corrected caches, window A, block means)

**TL;DR:** at k=5%: oracle 0.0188, coarse estimate 0.0194, simulated true-logits + predicted Gaussian noise
0.0189 (independent per head and step) and 0.0190 (one perturbation per key, shared by heads and steps)
— persistent key noise does NOT explain the gap
(measured/predicted noise std 1.02). The estimate misses 16.4% of the oracle tokens but only 3.8% of their mass;
56% of the missed tokens rank in the last 20% of the oracle set. Uncertainty bonus (rank by s_hat + c·sigma²): c=0.5 0.0193,
c=1 0.0193, c=2 0.0193. Matching the oracle at 5% needs k≈6.5%: 0.0190, 8%: 0.0188, 10%: 0.0186.

## Config
sigma_i = ||q|| g_k,i sqrt(D_c)/d (per head and token). 'sim' replaces the coarse logits by true logits + N(0, sigma_i²).
Rule: max over the GQA group of log-prob; window tokens excluded; error = attention-output rel err vs int8 reference.

